WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.040 --> 00:02.240
This series was created for entertainment purposes.

3
00:02.240 --> 00:05.680
The characters, actions, locations, dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

4
00:05.680 --> 00:08.120
and artistic elements depicted in this series

5
00:08.120 --> 00:10.040
are fictional and based on imagination,

6
00:10.040 --> 00:13.920
incorporating the beauty of the region's diverse cultures,

7
00:13.920 --> 00:18.400
including those of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

8
00:18.400 --> 00:20.560
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

9
00:20.560 --> 00:23.600
ethnic group, organization, profession, or group of individuals.

10
00:23.600 --> 00:26.040
Viewer discretion is advised.

11
00:26.040 --> 00:27.200
[Previously] Fongnuan.

12
00:27.200 --> 00:29.000
Who is... Fongnuan?

13
00:29.000 --> 00:30.120
Where is this place?

14
00:30.120 --> 00:31.200
Ullavee.

15
00:31.200 --> 00:33.440
Now that you've returned, I see how much you've grown.

16
00:33.440 --> 00:36.960
Thank you for your great support for the Crown Prince.

17
00:36.960 --> 00:38.200
You've just returned from the battlefield.

18
00:38.200 --> 00:41.400
Have you bathed in the sacred spring yet?

19
00:41.400 --> 00:46.120
Will bathing in the sacred spring make me a beloved son?

20
00:48.000 --> 00:49.640
Who are you?

21
00:53.960 --> 00:56.000
I'll pretend I never saw you here.

22
00:56.920 --> 00:59.200
You still have a life to live,

23
01:00.200 --> 01:02.400
so live it happily.

24
01:03.840 --> 01:05.960
"You still have a life to live,"

25
01:08.720 --> 01:11.080
"so live it happily."

26
01:13.040 --> 01:14.520
That's true.

27
01:16.960 --> 01:19.600
At least you're still alive, Na Boon.

28
01:21.040 --> 01:22.840
As for Fongnuan...

29
01:22.840 --> 01:26.360
Let's see what you've got.

30
01:33.120 --> 01:35.280
Pretty nice face.

31
01:35.280 --> 01:37.480
Clear skin, too.

32
01:37.480 --> 01:39.480
Much clearer than mine.

33
01:39.480 --> 01:42.000
Your hair is long too.

34
01:43.080 --> 01:45.160
It looks healthy.

35
01:45.160 --> 01:47.600
Long and thick too.

36
01:53.960 --> 01:56.320
Being you isn't so bad.

37
01:57.320 --> 01:58.760
Fongnuan.

38
02:00.200 --> 02:02.440
From now on,

39
02:03.680 --> 02:05.440
let's collab.

40
03:59.680 --> 04:04.520
[If You Can't Die, You Might As Well Be Happy]

41
04:15.800 --> 04:19.760
Lady Fongnuan, are you sure you want to go to the market looking like that?

42
04:24.520 --> 04:26.880
- Isn't it pretty? - Not pretty.

43
04:26.880 --> 04:28.960
You look like a madwoman.

44
04:28.960 --> 04:30.600
What do you mean?

45
04:30.600 --> 04:33.640
What woman in her right mind ties her hair like that?

46
04:33.640 --> 04:35.160
Only madwomen do.

47
04:35.160 --> 04:38.720
It's my hair. I can do whatever I want with it.

48
04:38.720 --> 04:40.840
This is called a braid.

49
04:42.080 --> 04:43.760
It's so pretty.

50
04:43.760 --> 04:45.440
- It's not. - It is!

51
04:45.440 --> 04:46.680
- It's not! - It is!

52
04:46.680 --> 04:47.840
- It's not. - It is!

53
04:47.840 --> 04:49.320
- It's not. - It is!

54
04:49.320 --> 04:50.640
It's not!

55
04:51.480 --> 04:53.440
You're the mad one!

56
04:53.440 --> 04:54.640
No, you are!

57
04:54.640 --> 04:58.280
You're calling someone else mad out of nowhere. You're the mad one.

58
04:58.280 --> 05:00.640
- You're the mad one. - You blind fool!

59
05:00.640 --> 05:02.080
You mad, blind fool!

60
05:02.080 --> 05:05.800
Whatever are you talking about? Have you gone mad?

61
05:05.800 --> 05:08.160
- You're the mad one! - Lady Fongnuan.

62
05:09.600 --> 05:11.320
He's a prince.

63
05:11.320 --> 05:14.880
You can't behave or speak to a prince like that.

64
05:19.120 --> 05:20.440
Sorry.

65
05:27.520 --> 05:29.840
Please accept my apologies, Your Highness.

66
05:29.840 --> 05:31.000
Ever since that day,

67
05:31.000 --> 05:34.760
Lady Fongnuan has yet to fully regain her wits.

68
05:39.400 --> 05:41.120
Lady Fongnuan.

69
05:41.120 --> 05:43.280
Mad and insolent.

70
07:29.680 --> 07:31.600
Red hibiscus.

71
07:32.920 --> 07:35.800
The real Courtesan House.

72
07:35.800 --> 07:38.360
I've only ever read about it in books.

73
07:39.800 --> 07:41.360
So this is what it's like in real life.

74
07:41.360 --> 07:43.680
That's called the Mhai flower.

75
07:44.560 --> 07:45.880
Lady Fongnuan,

76
07:45.880 --> 07:50.640
I don't think we should be hanging around outside the Courtesan House.

77
07:50.640 --> 07:53.400
The villagers will wag their tongues.

78
07:57.360 --> 07:58.920
Lady Fongnuan!

79
08:23.960 --> 08:25.200
Your Highness!

80
08:26.640 --> 08:29.800
Madwoman! Don't call me "Your Highness."

81
08:29.800 --> 08:32.000
And you mustn't tell anyone you saw me here!

82
08:34.240 --> 08:36.240
Why do you talk like Prince...

83
08:36.240 --> 08:39.400
I said you mustn't speak like that!

84
08:43.400 --> 08:46.880
- Why do you have to call me a madwoman? - Look at your hair.

85
08:46.880 --> 08:49.600
Look at you. You look like a madwoman.

86
08:49.600 --> 08:51.520
One moment you're here, the next you're somewhere else.

87
08:51.520 --> 08:55.400
If Saen Thep hadn't claimed you were Princess Maneethip's sister,

88
08:55.400 --> 08:58.320
you'd have been arrested and punished the day we met.

89
08:59.720 --> 09:01.360
Lady Fongnuan.

90
09:02.600 --> 09:05.480
Lady Fongnuan? Lady Fongnuan!

91
09:10.920 --> 09:12.360
Lady Fongnuan...

92
09:13.240 --> 09:14.560
who were you speaking with?

93
09:14.560 --> 09:17.440
- A madman. - A madman?

94
09:17.440 --> 09:21.600
Didn't I tell you not to come in here? You shouldn't be talking to a madman.

95
09:21.600 --> 09:25.280
- Why can't I? - It's unbecoming of a lady.

96
09:27.040 --> 09:30.760
I told you not to come in here. Let us go before someone sees us.

97
09:30.760 --> 09:31.880
We must hurry.

98
09:31.880 --> 09:35.120
Lha, we haven't even seen the inside. Must we leave now?

99
09:35.120 --> 09:37.440
- We must leave now! - We'll take our leave, then!

100
09:51.720 --> 09:54.160
That madwoman seems trustworthy enough.

101
10:06.720 --> 10:07.960
Lha...

102
10:09.400 --> 10:14.040
how lucky you are to be in Ullavee at this time.

103
10:18.160 --> 10:20.040
The weather is nice.

104
10:21.840 --> 10:24.160
There's no PM 2.5 pollution.

105
10:32.800 --> 10:35.080
Do you believe in reincarnation?

106
10:36.480 --> 10:37.960
As in,

107
10:38.680 --> 10:41.560
people dying and being reborn.

108
10:41.560 --> 10:44.400
Living many lifetimes, that sort of thing.

109
10:45.000 --> 10:47.080
Indeed, I do.

110
10:47.080 --> 10:49.800
We have 32 souls.

111
10:49.800 --> 10:52.400
In a sense, we all have 32 lives.

112
10:52.400 --> 10:54.000
So...

113
10:54.760 --> 10:56.760
the two of us...

114
10:57.960 --> 11:00.920
I guess our souls have been intertwined across many lifetimes.

115
11:02.640 --> 11:05.000
That's why we've met again in this life.

116
11:06.840 --> 11:09.160
How long have you been betraying me?

117
11:09.960 --> 11:11.520
Tell me!

118
11:12.840 --> 11:15.320
Boon, I... I...

119
11:15.320 --> 11:17.600
I'm sorry.

120
11:17.600 --> 11:19.760
I didn't mean to.

121
11:20.320 --> 11:23.800
- Boon, hear me out. I wasn't going to-- - Save it!

122
11:23.800 --> 11:26.320
You're just one guy. I don't care.

123
11:28.560 --> 11:32.520
- Hey, I'm sorry. - How could you do this to me?

124
11:32.520 --> 11:36.240
I really didn't mean to, Boon. I'm sorry.

125
11:36.240 --> 11:39.640
How long have we been friends, Eva?

126
11:40.800 --> 11:43.920
We can usually talk about anything, can't we?

127
11:45.920 --> 11:48.000
If you like him,

128
11:49.400 --> 11:51.120
you could've just told me.

129
11:52.560 --> 11:54.760
Boon, I'm really sorry.

130
11:54.760 --> 11:57.200
You're so heartless.

131
12:00.440 --> 12:02.280
It's fine.

132
12:02.280 --> 12:06.760
I'll just forget what happened.

133
12:07.560 --> 12:10.040
Let's start over, Eva.

134
12:12.920 --> 12:14.160
I mean, Lha.

135
12:17.120 --> 12:18.920
Yes.

136
12:18.920 --> 12:20.840
Let us start over, my lady.

137
12:22.600 --> 12:24.040
Okay.

138
12:24.040 --> 12:25.880
Deal.

139
12:25.880 --> 12:27.920
Right now, I'm Fongnuan.

140
12:27.920 --> 12:30.560
Eva, you're Lha.

141
12:31.760 --> 12:33.080
Yes.

142
12:34.120 --> 12:36.800
Are you quite well, Lady Fongnuan?

143
12:36.800 --> 12:38.520
Do you have a headache?

144
12:40.840 --> 12:43.240
I'm getting worried.

145
12:46.840 --> 12:48.800
I'm okay.

146
12:51.080 --> 12:53.320
I'm getting hungry.

147
12:53.320 --> 12:55.440
Let's go home.

148
12:55.440 --> 12:58.440
Ever since I woke up, I've been so stressed.

149
12:58.440 --> 13:01.200
I haven't had a proper meal.

150
13:01.200 --> 13:02.880
By the way,

151
13:02.880 --> 13:04.680
what's good to eat around here?

152
13:06.000 --> 13:08.560
- Well... - Never mind.

153
13:08.560 --> 13:11.160
- Let's go and find something to eat. - Yes.

154
13:11.160 --> 13:13.440
Lady Fongnuan, please wait for me.

155
13:33.800 --> 13:36.280
These look delicious.

156
13:36.280 --> 13:40.120
So... let me dig in!

157
13:40.840 --> 13:42.520
Wash your hands first.

158
13:54.360 --> 13:56.400
It's bad luck to take rice from the middle of the basket.

159
13:56.400 --> 13:59.680
We won't harvest enough rice to feed ourselves this year.

160
13:59.680 --> 14:01.360
Do you not remember?

161
14:02.400 --> 14:06.800
Then where should I take it from to make sure we have enough?

162
14:06.800 --> 14:08.800
Take it from the edge of the basket.

163
14:12.280 --> 14:14.400
Then shape it into a bite-sized ball.

164
14:16.960 --> 14:18.120
Wait.

165
14:18.120 --> 14:22.080
It's bad luck to bite into rice like that. You must shape it into a bite-sized ball.

166
14:23.320 --> 14:25.440
Bad luck again?

167
14:27.240 --> 14:30.160
No taking rice from the middle of the basket.

168
14:30.160 --> 14:32.040
No biting the rice.

169
14:32.040 --> 14:34.400
I'll remember that.

170
14:35.000 --> 14:38.280
Can I... eat now?

171
14:43.280 --> 14:45.360
Princess Maneethip,

172
14:45.360 --> 14:49.760
I don't think she's quite herself yet.

173
14:51.720 --> 14:54.360
Shall I summon a revered master

174
14:54.360 --> 14:56.880
to perform a Soul Recalling Ceremony for her, my lady?

175
14:56.880 --> 14:58.360
So delicious.

176
14:59.040 --> 15:01.480
You're an amazing cook.

177
15:02.280 --> 15:04.760
Sister Maneethip, you're amazing.

178
15:05.680 --> 15:07.560
Whatever are you talking about?

179
15:07.560 --> 15:09.720
Do not try to charm me.

180
15:09.720 --> 15:13.400
If you like it, then eat your fill. And eat properly.

181
15:14.680 --> 15:16.000
All right.

182
15:25.440 --> 15:27.840
Sister, eat.

183
15:27.840 --> 15:29.160
You go ahead.

184
15:29.160 --> 15:31.360
Do not blame me if I eat it all.

185
15:32.960 --> 15:34.120
Lha.

186
15:35.200 --> 15:36.960
I cannot, my lady.

187
15:38.080 --> 15:41.080
So... this is all for me?

188
15:52.240 --> 15:54.720
So much has happened in just one day.

189
15:56.000 --> 16:00.120
It'd be nice to at least see my mom while I'm here.

190
16:00.120 --> 16:02.520
I even saw Eva.

191
16:04.520 --> 16:07.240
Who knows what the future will bring?

192
16:08.840 --> 16:11.640
Whatever will be, will be, I guess.

193
16:18.320 --> 16:20.320
What language did you just speak?

194
16:25.040 --> 16:27.520
English, Your Highness.

195
16:27.520 --> 16:29.080
English?

196
16:30.000 --> 16:32.520
It's spoken by foreigners,

197
16:32.520 --> 16:37.240
the tall, fair-skinned,

198
16:37.240 --> 16:39.520
and golden-haired people.

199
16:39.520 --> 16:41.000
Westerners.

200
16:42.000 --> 16:43.640
I know them.

201
16:43.640 --> 16:45.920
I've heard merchants talk about them at the market.

202
16:46.840 --> 16:49.120
But how did you know their language?

203
16:52.400 --> 16:55.560
Ever since I awoke during the ceremony,

204
16:55.560 --> 16:58.320
I've somehow been able to speak it.

205
16:59.280 --> 17:01.880
I was probably punished by the guardian spirits.

206
17:04.160 --> 17:05.640
How strange.

207
17:06.240 --> 17:07.960
But that's good.

208
17:07.960 --> 17:09.880
Will you teach me sometime?

209
17:10.680 --> 17:12.240
Of course.

210
17:13.560 --> 17:17.920
Shall we... exchange favors?

211
17:19.800 --> 17:21.520
There are so many princes here.

212
17:21.520 --> 17:22.920
I still can't remember them all.

213
17:22.920 --> 17:26.720
I don't want to mistake anyone for someone else and get myself punished.

214
17:27.360 --> 17:31.520
Could you tell me who they are?

215
17:31.520 --> 17:33.960
I don't want to get into trouble again.

216
17:33.960 --> 17:36.720
Ullavee is a tributary kingdom.

217
17:36.720 --> 17:40.600
It's situated between three powerful empires.

218
17:40.600 --> 17:41.960
[Ullavee: The Forbidden Kingdom]

219
17:41.960 --> 17:45.240
The king's first son,

220
17:45.240 --> 17:50.800
our eldest brother is Prince Indraraja.

221
17:51.440 --> 17:55.800
He's the Crown Prince, or the heir to the throne.

222
17:56.400 --> 18:01.320
The first prince is the king's favorite.

223
18:01.320 --> 18:02.320
[6 Princes]

224
18:02.320 --> 18:04.080
The favorite child.

225
18:05.600 --> 18:10.240
What about you, Prince Saen Thep? What's your title?

226
18:10.240 --> 18:11.440
I'm the Third-in-Line.

227
18:11.440 --> 18:14.200
The second is wise in the management of state affairs.

228
18:14.200 --> 18:16.280
[2nd Prince: Manages State Affairs]

229
18:16.280 --> 18:19.720
The next one is Prince Kong Tai.

230
18:19.720 --> 18:21.880
Not pretty. You look like a madwoman.

231
18:21.880 --> 18:25.360
He's talkative. We're very close.

232
18:25.360 --> 18:27.920
He's the Fourth-in-Line.

233
18:27.920 --> 18:30.240
That one runs his mouth.

234
18:30.240 --> 18:34.320
The third one has a keen interest in astronomy.

235
18:34.880 --> 18:38.320
Is there any prince who enjoys going out and about?

236
18:39.680 --> 18:41.480
That's Prince Fah Haam.

237
18:42.920 --> 18:46.680
He has no seat on the royal council that governs the kingdom.

238
18:46.680 --> 18:48.160
An artist.

239
18:48.160 --> 18:49.440
[4th Prince: Artist]

240
18:49.440 --> 18:53.400
The youngest prince is Prince Jom Harn.

241
18:53.400 --> 18:55.520
He's the Fifth-in-Line.

242
18:56.400 --> 18:58.760
The fifth prince is skilled in combat.

243
18:58.760 --> 19:00.480
[5th Prince: Combat]

244
19:00.480 --> 19:02.920
Is that all?

245
19:02.920 --> 19:04.800
There's one more.

246
19:04.800 --> 19:08.600
Is he tall, with a stern face, an intimidating look,

247
19:08.600 --> 19:11.000
and scars all over his body?

248
19:12.040 --> 19:14.280
You know my brother Mueang Fah?

249
19:15.400 --> 19:17.640
Prince Mueang Fah.

250
19:19.000 --> 19:22.400
He was sent to a city on the border as a child.

251
19:22.400 --> 19:26.680
How do you know he has scars all over his body?

252
19:30.120 --> 19:31.960
I...

253
19:31.960 --> 19:36.240
I've heard people talk about it.

254
19:36.240 --> 19:39.120
So there are six princes, correct?

255
19:40.720 --> 19:44.440
Most of the princes have different mothers,

256
19:44.440 --> 19:46.640
but they've been close since childhood.

257
19:46.640 --> 19:49.840
Still, no matter how close they are,

258
19:49.840 --> 19:54.920
the fight for power can get brutal.

259
19:56.160 --> 19:59.560
Prince Indraraja, Prince Saen Thep,

260
19:59.560 --> 20:05.040
Prince Kong Tai, Prince Fah Haam, Prince Jom Harn, and Prince Mueang Fah.

261
20:05.040 --> 20:11.160
Ullavee reached its greatest prosperity under...

262
20:11.160 --> 20:13.840
Phaya Devaraja,

263
20:13.840 --> 20:18.640
its last and most ruthless king.

264
20:19.360 --> 20:24.200
He seized the throne by murdering his own siblings.

265
20:27.960 --> 20:30.680
Who's Phaya Devaraja?

266
20:38.920 --> 20:41.920
Seer Phrommaya has chosen an auspicious time for the bedding ceremony.

267
20:41.920 --> 20:44.360
We only have a few days to prepare.

268
20:44.360 --> 20:46.680
After the Soul-Blessing Ceremony,

269
20:46.680 --> 20:50.720
your father and I will escort the two of you to the bridal chamber.

270
20:50.720 --> 20:55.520
The ceremony must be grand and flawless,

271
20:55.520 --> 21:00.200
worthy of Saen Thep, a prince of Ullavee.

272
21:02.280 --> 21:04.240
Maneethip,

273
21:04.240 --> 21:06.520
I will have the maids from the powder room

274
21:06.520 --> 21:09.720
oil your hair, scrub your skin,

275
21:09.720 --> 21:12.240
steam your body, and apply a face mask.

276
21:12.240 --> 21:16.480
Everyone there should be in awe of you,

277
21:16.480 --> 21:24.040
and see that Saen Thep has chosen a consort worthy of him.

278
21:28.040 --> 21:29.240
Yes.

279
21:31.000 --> 21:36.360
Tomorrow, the king will send gold-thread silk and jewelry from Wiang Kaew

280
21:36.360 --> 21:38.680
for you to choose from.

281
21:39.440 --> 21:41.120
Yes.

282
21:41.120 --> 21:45.080
Everything must be done with the dignity our station demands.

283
21:45.720 --> 21:48.960
Once Saen Thep becomes King,

284
21:49.520 --> 21:52.080
you shall be Queen.

285
21:52.080 --> 21:54.200
Let us get through this ceremony first, Mother.

286
21:54.200 --> 21:57.080
Her face turns pale just talking about the preparations.

287
21:57.080 --> 21:59.440
Do not think of her as Queen just yet.

288
21:59.440 --> 22:01.840
Let her first learn to be a good consort.

289
22:01.840 --> 22:05.360
All I've heard her say is "Yes. Yes. Yes."

290
22:05.360 --> 22:07.840
Maneethip must be nervous

291
22:07.840 --> 22:10.360
about such an important ceremony.

292
22:10.360 --> 22:12.480
That's why she's been paying such close attention.

293
22:14.320 --> 22:18.360
The truth is, you're happy about this too,

294
22:21.640 --> 22:23.200
are you not?

295
22:27.720 --> 22:28.920
Yes.

296
22:30.000 --> 22:31.720
Come with me.

297
22:31.720 --> 22:35.040
We will have the wardrobe maids take your measurements

298
22:35.040 --> 22:37.840
so we can prepare the right tube skirt for you.

299
22:37.840 --> 22:39.080
Yes.

300
22:54.080 --> 22:56.480
Are you sure, Saen Thep,

301
22:56.480 --> 23:00.280
this is the woman you fell in love with at first sight?

302
23:00.280 --> 23:02.880
The one you rushed home

303
23:02.880 --> 23:06.200
to ask Father to arrange a marriage with?

304
23:06.200 --> 23:08.520
Are you sure you've got the right woman?

305
23:37.680 --> 23:41.160
Lady Fongnuan, your skirt is flying up!

306
23:42.240 --> 23:43.520
- See? - Lady Fongnuan!

307
23:43.520 --> 23:45.200
- It's not hard at all. - Careful, my lady.

308
23:46.640 --> 23:49.240
- Watch me, Lha. - Yesterday, I managed to do this five times.

309
23:49.240 --> 23:51.600
- Please be careful. - Lady Fongnuan.

310
23:51.600 --> 23:54.080
- Your skirt is flying up. - Look!

311
23:54.080 --> 23:56.480
Come on. I'm going to let the ball go.

312
23:56.480 --> 24:00.400
Ready, Lha? One, two, three! Here!

313
24:03.400 --> 24:05.040
I'm fine.

314
24:05.040 --> 24:09.320
I think we should stop. If Princess Maneethip sees us, she'll scold us.

315
24:09.320 --> 24:11.680
I can play by myself. You sit and rest, Lha.

316
24:11.680 --> 24:13.480
- Lady Fongnuan! - Fongnuan.

317
24:14.120 --> 24:15.400
Lha.

318
24:16.880 --> 24:18.520
Stop playing already.

319
24:18.520 --> 24:19.920
Come back inside.

320
24:20.960 --> 24:22.280
My lady.

321
24:30.040 --> 24:31.360
Please stop, my lady.

322
24:31.360 --> 24:33.160
Princess Maneethip has come to fetch us back inside.

323
24:33.160 --> 24:35.240
Lha!

324
24:35.960 --> 24:37.680
It's time to go, my lady.

325
24:40.280 --> 24:43.480
- Lady Fongnuan! - I know.

326
25:08.840 --> 25:10.320
I'm full.

327
25:15.480 --> 25:17.560
Are you so excited after discussing

328
25:17.560 --> 25:20.000
the bedding ceremony that you've lost your appetite?

329
25:25.720 --> 25:27.760
Quite the opposite.

330
25:50.680 --> 25:51.840
Lha,

331
25:54.280 --> 25:57.080
why doesn't she seem excited?

332
25:57.080 --> 25:58.720
That's unusual.

333
25:59.400 --> 26:01.920
Do you not remember, Lady Fongnuan?

334
26:06.080 --> 26:08.560
I must have forgotten a few things.

335
26:09.680 --> 26:11.800
Could you tell me?

336
26:11.800 --> 26:14.720
I cannot speak of my masters' affairs.

337
26:16.040 --> 26:18.320
It is for the best that you do not remember.

338
26:19.840 --> 26:23.000
If you don't tell me, I'll ask her myself.

339
26:23.000 --> 26:24.560
Please don't, my lady.

340
26:26.800 --> 26:30.440
If you don't want Princess Maneethip to suffer any more,

341
26:30.440 --> 26:32.560
please don't ask her.

342
26:32.560 --> 26:34.400
I beg you.

343
27:14.440 --> 27:17.520
Prince Saen Thep seems like a good man.

344
27:17.520 --> 27:22.880
He's kind, patient, and he seems to love her dearly.

345
27:25.480 --> 27:27.920
If I were her,

346
27:27.920 --> 27:29.640
I'd be happy.

347
28:54.880 --> 28:56.640
If one day,

348
28:59.120 --> 29:01.960
I earn enough money to buy back your freedom,

349
29:02.920 --> 29:04.840
let us get out of here...

350
29:06.160 --> 29:08.920
and start a new life together, Nam Nang.

351
29:08.920 --> 29:11.000
My price is rather high.

352
29:12.360 --> 29:14.840
Where would a musician like you...

353
29:14.840 --> 29:17.440
find the money to buy my freedom?

354
29:26.600 --> 29:28.760
What if I could?

355
29:35.120 --> 29:39.880
Getting to the top here was no easy feat.

356
29:39.880 --> 29:44.920
You want me to leave everything and start over?

357
29:44.920 --> 29:46.400
Why?

358
29:53.360 --> 29:55.640
Because of my love.

359
30:02.920 --> 30:05.080
Love does not exist.

360
30:06.600 --> 30:09.080
There is only pleasure and desire,

361
30:09.760 --> 30:12.360
and the bonds that time and fate create.

362
30:16.480 --> 30:19.400
I will not risk my life.

363
30:19.400 --> 30:21.680
The outside world is frightening.

364
30:23.600 --> 30:28.320
No amount of love can withstand it.

365
30:31.880 --> 30:34.200
If you love me,

366
30:38.080 --> 30:40.560
then simply come and see me here.

367
30:52.120 --> 30:54.080
If I have to pay the tribute twice,

368
30:54.080 --> 30:57.320
how am I supposed to make a profit from my business?

369
30:57.320 --> 31:01.760
This is Crown Prince Indraraja's order. Do you dare defy it?

370
31:02.320 --> 31:07.160
If you have so many problems, then pack up and go home.

371
31:08.240 --> 31:11.520
And do not expect to trade in Ullavee again.

372
31:12.320 --> 31:16.040
No, Your Highness. I'm just surprised, that's all.

373
31:16.040 --> 31:20.000
I have never heard of such a rule in Ullavee.

374
31:21.240 --> 31:23.280
There are bandits all along the border these days,

375
31:23.280 --> 31:26.120
waiting to rob passing caravans.

376
31:26.120 --> 31:29.640
Without protection tribute,

377
31:29.640 --> 31:33.720
Crown Prince Indraraja won't send soldiers to guard your caravan.

378
31:35.480 --> 31:38.760
Are you sure you can fend for yourselves?

379
31:50.440 --> 31:57.520
Here is the tribute from our caravan. We ask for Crown Prince Indraraja's protection.

380
31:59.080 --> 32:01.160
I assure you,

381
32:01.160 --> 32:05.240
your caravan will remain safe and sound.

382
32:16.160 --> 32:17.520
And...

383
32:19.000 --> 32:20.360
what of you?

384
32:44.960 --> 32:47.200
Listen, all of you.

385
32:47.200 --> 32:52.480
From now on, anyone wishing to trade in Ullavee

386
32:52.480 --> 32:56.480
must pay tribute to Crown Prince Indraraja.

387
32:56.480 --> 32:58.600
There will be no exceptions.

388
33:00.640 --> 33:02.600
The Crown Prince...

389
33:02.600 --> 33:05.320
is demanding tribute for protection?

390
33:05.320 --> 33:07.440
It is nothing unusual.

391
33:07.440 --> 33:10.000
I've seen it time and time again.

392
33:10.000 --> 33:12.560
Nobles bribe their way into positions of power.

393
33:13.160 --> 33:16.880
Merchants pay protection fees to trade.

394
33:16.880 --> 33:21.040
The powerful find plenty of ways to profit from their positions.

395
33:21.040 --> 33:25.240
If they collect tribute and pocket it

396
33:25.240 --> 33:27.840
instead of handing it over to the Royal Treasury,

397
33:27.840 --> 33:30.000
that's a crime.

398
33:30.000 --> 33:32.320
That is the outside world for you.

399
33:33.720 --> 33:38.560
The powerful extort money from ordinary people without fear of the law.

400
33:38.560 --> 33:41.160
Even caravan merchants face this much oppression.

401
33:41.160 --> 33:45.160
Imagine how much worse off I'd be.

402
33:49.600 --> 33:52.440
Not all nobles are like that.

403
33:55.080 --> 33:58.000
You speak as if you're one of them.

404
35:09.200 --> 35:12.600
My sister asked me to return the unused fabric.

405
35:14.680 --> 35:16.560
Come, sit up here.

406
35:22.600 --> 35:24.840
Have you chosen yours?

407
35:26.160 --> 35:29.840
The king picked these out for you and my sister.

408
35:29.840 --> 35:33.680
I couldn't possibly wear them. I don't want to get too big for my boots.

409
35:34.240 --> 35:36.160
Too big for your boots?

410
35:38.600 --> 35:46.000
- What does that have to do with anything? - I'm talking nonsense again, aren't I?

411
35:46.000 --> 35:47.440
It's all right.

412
35:47.440 --> 35:50.760
Go ahead and say it. It's actually quite funny.

413
35:50.760 --> 35:55.080
It's better than before, when you wouldn't say a word.

414
35:55.080 --> 35:58.720
I was mute before, so now I'm mad instead.

415
36:14.240 --> 36:16.000
Was I smiling too much?

416
36:17.080 --> 36:19.160
Is that why you're making that face?

417
36:19.160 --> 36:21.400
It's nice to see you smile.

418
36:21.400 --> 36:24.160
Much better than when you give me a stern look.

419
36:25.480 --> 36:31.280
If you hadn't made me worry at the ceremony,

420
36:31.280 --> 36:32.720
I wouldn't have scolded you.

421
36:35.920 --> 36:37.400
Let me pick one for you.

422
37:00.680 --> 37:02.640
This one suits you.

423
37:04.960 --> 37:06.800
It looks vibrant.

424
37:08.280 --> 37:09.680
It's yours.

425
37:10.680 --> 37:12.360
Thank you.

426
37:33.080 --> 37:35.320
You and your sister are...

427
37:36.600 --> 37:37.760
strange.

428
37:40.160 --> 37:42.560
The first time I met Maneethip,

429
37:43.520 --> 37:47.640
she was cheerful and full of life.

430
37:49.840 --> 37:51.440
But you were quiet.

431
37:52.080 --> 37:54.080
You wouldn't say a word.

432
37:54.080 --> 37:56.560
You looked weary and listless.

433
37:58.240 --> 37:59.760
But now,

434
38:00.560 --> 38:02.320
it's like you and Maneethip...

435
38:03.200 --> 38:05.360
switched bodies.

436
38:06.920 --> 38:09.000
Maneethip has grown quiet,

437
38:09.880 --> 38:15.320
while you... never fail to make me smile.

438
38:20.480 --> 38:21.880
Fongnuan.

439
38:22.880 --> 38:24.440
Fongnuan.

440
38:26.240 --> 38:27.520
Yes?

441
38:29.080 --> 38:31.080
I have to head to the Royal Library.

442
38:31.080 --> 38:33.800
I have a meeting with Seer Phrommaya.

443
38:33.800 --> 38:36.000
Please take that piece of fabric

444
38:36.000 --> 38:38.560
and tell Maneethip I wanted you to have it.

445
38:38.560 --> 38:41.120
I look forward to seeing you wear it on the day of the ceremony.

446
38:43.080 --> 38:44.640
Thank you.

447
39:28.080 --> 39:30.520
You can't feel like this, Boon.

448
39:33.040 --> 39:35.160
You're Fongnuan now.

449
39:58.080 --> 39:59.800
A birthday celebration?

450
40:00.520 --> 40:01.840
Yes.

451
40:02.520 --> 40:05.760
I have much to attend to before my ceremony.

452
40:05.760 --> 40:09.640
I'd like you to prepare a gift for Prince Kong Tai on my behalf.

453
40:11.000 --> 40:14.400
What kind of gifts do people give each other here?

454
40:14.400 --> 40:18.080
Prince Saen Thep said Prince Kong Tai is having bad luck.

455
40:18.080 --> 40:21.440
I think a Hawk's Eye Amulet may be a good idea.

456
40:22.280 --> 40:23.800
A Hawk's Eye Amulet?

457
40:24.400 --> 40:26.280
What is that?

458
40:27.000 --> 40:30.240
It's an amulet to ward off evil.

459
40:30.240 --> 40:32.680
It's made from bamboo strips

460
40:32.680 --> 40:34.560
woven into the shape of a hawk's eye.

461
40:36.320 --> 40:40.640
That sounds like a good idea. Where can we buy a Hawk's Eye Amulet?

462
40:40.640 --> 40:42.520
There's no need to buy it.

463
40:42.520 --> 40:45.840
You can make one yourself. It's very easy.

464
40:48.200 --> 40:51.040
The scrubbing is done. Now, let us rinse you off.

465
40:51.800 --> 40:53.360
Lha,

466
40:53.360 --> 40:56.000
please help Fongnuan make a Hawk's Eye Amulet.

467
40:56.000 --> 40:57.120
Yes, my lady.

468
40:57.120 --> 41:01.320
Fongnuan, do not be too mischievous and do not make me worry.

469
41:01.320 --> 41:04.280
- Do you understand? - Yes, sister.

470
41:05.080 --> 41:07.680
Go on, and be back soon.

471
41:07.680 --> 41:09.320
Before nightfall.

472
41:09.320 --> 41:10.480
Very well.

473
41:16.800 --> 41:21.080
Lha, is a Hawk's Eye Amulet really easy to make?

474
41:26.360 --> 41:28.880
You call this easy?

475
41:29.760 --> 41:32.520
It's not difficult at all, my lady. Please give it a try.

476
41:32.520 --> 41:37.200
Choose straight bamboo so we can get straight strips.

477
41:39.040 --> 41:41.280
Will this one do?

478
41:41.280 --> 41:45.240
Lady Fongnuan, aim, then chop.

479
41:45.240 --> 41:47.840
Aim, then chop?

480
41:47.840 --> 41:49.000
Yes.

481
41:53.280 --> 41:55.520
Could you use a little more force?

482
41:57.280 --> 42:00.720
A little more force, please. A little more.

483
42:11.120 --> 42:14.880
I think we should go cut down that clump of bamboo over there.

484
42:14.880 --> 42:17.280
They're all straight stalks.

485
42:17.280 --> 42:21.120
Leave this here for now.

486
42:21.120 --> 42:23.040
Let us go.

487
42:23.040 --> 42:24.600
- Lha! - Please follow me.

488
42:24.600 --> 42:27.440
Lha, wait! Lha, wait!

489
42:27.440 --> 42:29.080
This way!

490
42:32.760 --> 42:34.400
Lha, wait for me!

491
42:36.360 --> 42:38.760
Lha! Wait for me!

492
42:40.200 --> 42:42.560
Lady Fongnuan, follow me quickly!

493
42:43.400 --> 42:45.280
Wait for me!

494
42:47.680 --> 42:49.440
Lha!

495
42:53.480 --> 42:55.920
This way, Lady Fongnuan! This way!

496
42:58.560 --> 43:00.160
Right this way!

497
43:01.200 --> 43:02.480
Lha!

498
43:02.480 --> 43:03.560
I found it, Lady Fongnuan!

499
43:03.560 --> 43:05.480
- This way! - Lha, wait!

500
43:05.480 --> 43:07.640
- There it is! - Lha!

501
43:07.640 --> 43:09.520
Lha, wait!

502
43:09.520 --> 43:11.000
Lady Fongnuan!

503
43:12.600 --> 43:13.720
Lady Fongnuan?

504
43:13.720 --> 43:17.800
Lha, I'm here.

505
43:17.800 --> 43:19.400
Lady Fongnuan!

506
43:21.720 --> 43:23.760
Lady Fongnuan! Are you hurt?

507
43:23.760 --> 43:26.560
This way. Can you get up, my lady?

508
43:27.320 --> 43:28.960
Careful.

509
43:32.120 --> 43:34.720
Lady Fongnuan! Are you hurt anywhere?

510
43:36.320 --> 43:38.720
You didn't wait for me.

511
43:38.720 --> 43:41.240
I'm sorry, my lady.

512
43:41.240 --> 43:43.120
You're not hurt, are you?

513
43:49.320 --> 43:52.840
We're lucky this animal trap is old.

514
43:53.720 --> 43:58.720
Otherwise, those sharpened bamboo stakes could've impaled you.

515
44:01.880 --> 44:04.040
I almost died.

516
44:04.040 --> 44:07.960
Let me cut the bamboo myself.

517
44:07.960 --> 44:10.320
Please wait for me here, my lady.

518
44:14.200 --> 44:16.520
Stay here. Don't go anywhere.

519
44:16.520 --> 44:17.880
I'll stay right here.

520
44:20.120 --> 44:21.640
Come back soon.

521
44:21.640 --> 44:22.880
Yes, my lady.

522
44:36.440 --> 44:38.160
Hey! That way!

523
44:40.000 --> 44:41.880
Hey! Stop!

524
44:53.360 --> 44:54.760
Stop right there!

525
44:58.880 --> 45:01.800
There! After him! Come on!

526
45:01.800 --> 45:04.320
- Stop right there! - Stop!

527
45:07.600 --> 45:11.960
- Hey! Stop! - Hey, stop right there! Hey!

528
45:12.560 --> 45:15.280
- He's going that way! - Stop right there!

529
45:18.920 --> 45:21.840
Your Highness! Your Highness!

530
45:21.840 --> 45:23.200
Come here!

531
45:36.760 --> 45:37.920
Down!

532
45:37.920 --> 45:40.120
- Stop! - Stop right there!

533
45:42.640 --> 45:44.480
Hey! Stop!

534
45:44.480 --> 45:47.240
- Stop right there! - Hey! Stop!

535
45:48.480 --> 45:50.120
Where did he go?

536
45:50.120 --> 45:51.360
Hey, you.

537
45:52.040 --> 45:56.080
- Did you see a young man come this way? - You mean the shirtless one?

538
45:56.080 --> 46:01.720
He went that way. He was running so fast. He must be long gone by now. Hurry after him.

539
46:01.720 --> 46:04.360
- Let's go! Hurry after him! - Move!

540
46:10.280 --> 46:11.920
You trust people too easily.

541
46:12.960 --> 46:14.080
Your Highness!

542
46:16.240 --> 46:18.560
Your Highness! You're safe now.

543
46:20.960 --> 46:22.120
They're gone.

544
46:39.240 --> 46:40.640
Thanks.

545
46:44.400 --> 46:46.200
You're the madwoman.

546
46:46.800 --> 46:49.160
I'm not.

547
46:49.160 --> 46:51.080
I'm tired of explaining.

548
46:52.840 --> 46:55.960
What did you do, anyway?

549
46:55.960 --> 46:58.000
Why were they chasing you?

550
47:02.560 --> 47:06.040
Whoever ends up with the most marks... loses.

551
47:17.480 --> 47:21.840
You knew they were drugging their opponents.

552
47:21.840 --> 47:23.680
So why get involved?

553
47:32.960 --> 47:37.080
- Come on! Go! - Come on!

554
47:37.080 --> 47:38.840
- Go! - Go!

555
47:38.840 --> 47:40.720
- Fight! - Fight!

556
47:40.720 --> 47:42.560
- Get him! - Come on!

557
47:42.560 --> 47:44.800
- Get him! - Get in there!

558
47:44.800 --> 47:46.040
- Get him! - Get him!

559
47:46.040 --> 47:49.120
- Hurry up! - Get him!

560
47:51.880 --> 47:54.200
Get up!

561
47:54.200 --> 47:55.640
Fight!

562
47:59.880 --> 48:01.360
Hit him!

563
48:03.520 --> 48:06.480
- Get up! - Get up!

564
48:06.480 --> 48:07.960
Watch out!

565
48:09.000 --> 48:10.680
- Fight! Fight! - Fight! Fight!

566
48:11.400 --> 48:13.080
- Fight! - Fight!

567
48:13.080 --> 48:15.360
- Fight! - Fight!

568
48:23.080 --> 48:25.080
- Fight! - Fight!

569
48:25.080 --> 48:27.200
Fight!

570
48:27.200 --> 48:30.320
Fight! Fight! Fight!

571
48:30.320 --> 48:32.680
Come on! Get up!

572
48:32.680 --> 48:36.480
Hey! Come on! Nice!

573
48:36.480 --> 48:39.880
Go! Come on!

574
48:42.040 --> 48:43.360
Keep going!

575
48:44.160 --> 48:45.560
He's losing!

576
48:52.080 --> 48:53.760
- Go! - Go!

577
48:55.560 --> 48:57.320
- Get up! - Keep going!

578
49:05.000 --> 49:06.800
Damn it!

579
49:08.000 --> 49:09.720
You cheated!

580
49:09.720 --> 49:12.120
Hey! How could you possibly lose?

581
49:12.120 --> 49:14.760
- I made him drink the water. - I saw him drink it with my own eyes.

582
49:14.760 --> 49:17.040
Damn it! How could you lose?

583
49:19.880 --> 49:21.480
Hey!

584
49:21.480 --> 49:23.520
Where do you think you're going? Stop!

585
49:23.520 --> 49:26.040
- Hey, stop! - Hey!

586
49:26.040 --> 49:27.040
Stop!

587
49:27.040 --> 49:30.280
Come on! Come on, winners!

588
49:31.080 --> 49:32.920
Tough luck, losers!

589
49:35.000 --> 49:38.720
If you hadn't run into me, they would've beaten you up.

590
49:38.720 --> 49:40.400
Then what would you have done?

591
49:44.200 --> 49:47.560
You're... quite clever.

592
49:47.560 --> 49:51.280
You saved me without anyone getting hurt.

593
49:52.280 --> 49:55.760
I'm in your debt this time.

594
49:55.760 --> 49:57.440
Tell me how I can repay you.

595
49:57.440 --> 50:01.440
No need. It's nothing.

596
50:01.440 --> 50:05.240
Just stop calling me a madwoman. That's all.

597
50:13.120 --> 50:15.600
Your face looks younger than mine.

598
50:15.600 --> 50:17.720
So I'll call you...

599
50:20.360 --> 50:21.920
junior.

600
50:24.200 --> 50:27.480
And you shall call me...

601
50:27.480 --> 50:28.840
senior.

602
50:30.160 --> 50:31.960
All right.

603
50:31.960 --> 50:33.360
Deal.

604
50:36.040 --> 50:37.640
Deal?

605
50:37.640 --> 50:40.480
"Deal," like this. Not like that.

606
50:41.800 --> 50:43.680
Deal.

607
50:44.440 --> 50:46.480
- Deal. - Deal.

608
50:48.560 --> 50:49.640
Here.

609
50:50.600 --> 50:54.000
It means we're agreed.

610
50:54.000 --> 50:55.080
- Deal. - Deal.

611
50:55.080 --> 50:56.800
- Deal. - Deal.

612
50:56.800 --> 50:59.120
- Deal. - Deal.

613
50:59.120 --> 51:00.720
- Deal. - Deal.

614
51:00.720 --> 51:01.800
Deal.

615
51:02.520 --> 51:03.440
That's enough.

616
51:03.440 --> 51:05.280
- Deal. - That's enough.

617
51:20.280 --> 51:23.280
You should hurry along before those men return.

618
51:25.200 --> 51:28.280
I... shall take my leave then,

619
51:28.880 --> 51:30.120
junior.

620
51:36.040 --> 51:37.640
I'm back.

621
51:38.480 --> 51:40.040
I'm back, my lady.

622
51:41.760 --> 51:45.480
Lha! Do we really have to carry this much back?

623
51:45.480 --> 51:47.240
This is not all.

624
51:56.440 --> 51:59.080
- Where does she get all that energy? - Lady Fongnuan! Watch out!

625
52:00.200 --> 52:01.720
Lha!

626
52:04.920 --> 52:07.600
- That's enough. - That's not all.

627
52:07.600 --> 52:10.960
Lha! I can't carry all this.

628
52:22.760 --> 52:24.320
How infuriating.

629
52:33.360 --> 52:34.400
- Get up! - Get up!

630
52:34.400 --> 52:36.160
- Hey! Hey! - Get up!

631
52:36.160 --> 52:39.640
- Let go! - Let go of me! Let go of me!

632
52:39.640 --> 52:42.680
Hey! Let go!

633
52:42.680 --> 52:44.080
Let go of me!

634
52:52.320 --> 52:53.880
- Let go! - Bring them in.

635
52:53.880 --> 52:55.200
Let go of me!

636
52:55.200 --> 52:58.000
- Let go! - Sit down!

637
52:58.000 --> 52:59.560
These are the men

638
52:59.560 --> 53:02.600
who ambushed our caravan and stole our livestock.

639
53:02.600 --> 53:04.920
How dare you steal what is mine?

640
53:05.760 --> 53:07.440
Aren't you afraid to die?

641
53:12.440 --> 53:14.040
Those are mine.

642
53:14.040 --> 53:17.640
You and Prince Indraraja stole them from me!

643
53:18.840 --> 53:22.120
Trade has been so difficult that I have nothing left.

644
53:23.640 --> 53:26.080
I'd rather fight to the death than starve!

645
53:28.200 --> 53:31.600
The whole of Ullavee and Merng Mang will hear

646
53:31.600 --> 53:36.280
that Crown Princes like you two are deceitful

647
53:36.280 --> 53:37.840
and exploit us common folk!

648
53:55.520 --> 53:57.520
People like you...

649
53:58.200 --> 54:00.560
have no right to negotiate with me.

650
54:01.400 --> 54:02.800
Low-born churl.

651
55:17.120 --> 55:19.840
When I went to the Courtesan House,

652
55:19.840 --> 55:23.920
I saw Pha Wiang use Indraraja's name

653
55:24.600 --> 55:29.960
to extort protection money from Siao caravan merchants.

654
55:33.440 --> 55:35.160
Then suddenly,

655
55:35.160 --> 55:39.520
the merchants were dragged away.

656
55:39.520 --> 55:42.600
I had a bad feeling, so I followed them.

657
55:42.600 --> 55:44.520
When I found them again, they were already dead.

658
55:47.400 --> 55:49.680
This is a grave matter, Mueang Fah.

659
55:52.960 --> 55:56.240
Why are you telling me this?

660
55:56.240 --> 55:59.200
I believe you love Ullavee

661
55:59.800 --> 56:04.280
and won't let someone like Prince Pha Wiang from Merng Mang

662
56:04.280 --> 56:06.200
profit off our kingdom.

663
56:11.840 --> 56:13.680
Why do you believe so?

664
56:14.440 --> 56:15.960
My heart tells me so.

665
56:17.560 --> 56:20.760
I haven't told anyone else about this but you.

666
56:21.960 --> 56:25.560
What you do next is up to you.

667
56:25.560 --> 56:27.800
This matter requires careful thought.

668
56:34.040 --> 56:35.640
By the way,

669
56:38.320 --> 56:40.760
what were you doing at the Courtesan House?

670
56:42.480 --> 56:45.720
A prince sneaking off to the Courtesan House is wrong.

671
56:46.560 --> 56:49.040
It's a serious violation of the Royal Residence's rules.

672
56:49.040 --> 56:53.000
If someone sees you and word gets back to the king,

673
56:53.000 --> 56:54.920
you will be severely punished.

674
56:55.640 --> 56:58.320
I just happened to be passing by.

675
56:58.320 --> 56:59.600
You're lying.

676
57:07.120 --> 57:09.560
What I did is of no consequence.

677
57:10.880 --> 57:14.360
At least I got valuable information for the kingdom.

678
57:17.560 --> 57:21.880
I couldn't have caught the thieves without entering their den.

679
57:25.480 --> 57:29.120
I ask that you keep this a secret

680
57:29.720 --> 57:34.240
until we know for certain whether Indraraja is involved.

681
57:39.160 --> 57:41.240
You may go.

682
57:41.240 --> 57:43.480
I'll take care of the bodies.

683
59:24.960 --> 59:27.640
Someone saw Pha Wiang using your name

684
59:28.280 --> 59:31.480
to collect protection tribute from the caravan merchants.

685
59:32.560 --> 59:34.720
He threatened that if they didn't pay,

686
59:35.440 --> 59:38.680
you wouldn't send soldiers to protect them

687
59:38.680 --> 59:40.720
from the bandits at the border.

688
59:46.200 --> 59:48.000
Who told you this?

689
59:52.320 --> 59:53.720
A well-wisher.

690
59:58.320 --> 01:00:00.040
Do you believe them?

691
01:00:04.280 --> 01:00:07.760
I don't care if it's true or not.

692
01:00:10.960 --> 01:00:15.480
A little extorted money from the common folk?

693
01:00:15.480 --> 01:00:17.280
I have no desire for that.

694
01:00:18.000 --> 01:00:20.320
I don't believe Pha Wiang did it.

695
01:00:21.040 --> 01:00:24.600
What you've heard is false.

696
01:00:27.360 --> 01:00:31.080
But there were witnesses, and some people died.

697
01:00:32.480 --> 01:00:35.640
Collecting tribute is one thing.

698
01:00:36.640 --> 01:00:39.520
But merchants from Siao have died.

699
01:00:40.240 --> 01:00:42.560
If this escalates

700
01:00:42.560 --> 01:00:45.880
and affects relations between our cities,

701
01:00:45.880 --> 01:00:47.880
it will become a serious matter.

702
01:00:52.200 --> 01:00:55.280
I'd like you to see this matter properly resolved.

703
01:00:58.920 --> 01:01:01.640
In the future, you will rule Ullavee.

704
01:01:03.280 --> 01:01:05.360
If this is true,

705
01:01:06.040 --> 01:01:08.360
it's not worth risking your throne.

706
01:01:09.760 --> 01:01:14.640
But if you have no part in this, you would do well to be cautious,

707
01:01:15.200 --> 01:01:19.800
for what Pha Wiang did is serious.

708
01:01:25.960 --> 01:01:30.320
This time, I'll risk my life to hide the truth.

709
01:01:31.760 --> 01:01:34.240
But let this be the last time.

710
01:01:44.320 --> 01:01:46.520
I will see to this myself.

711
01:01:46.520 --> 01:01:48.280
If it is true,

712
01:01:49.120 --> 01:01:52.320
I will not let it tarnish my honor.

713
01:02:20.400 --> 01:02:24.360
All of this is for you.

714
01:02:25.240 --> 01:02:26.920
You've done very well.

715
01:02:39.680 --> 01:02:45.240
All this money and these valuables will secure your Crown Prince title.

716
01:02:45.240 --> 01:02:47.160
It will never be shaken.

717
01:02:48.040 --> 01:02:51.920
Whatever it takes to help you take the Ullavee throne,

718
01:02:51.920 --> 01:02:53.960
I'm willing to do it.

719
01:02:54.680 --> 01:02:56.160
Thank you, brother.

720
01:02:57.400 --> 01:02:59.920
But be careful next time.

721
01:03:00.520 --> 01:03:02.960
Someone's watching us.

722
01:03:04.080 --> 01:03:05.600
Is it Mueang Fah?

723
01:03:06.720 --> 01:03:08.040
It's someone else.

724
01:03:10.440 --> 01:03:13.040
But Mueang Fah came to warn me

725
01:03:13.680 --> 01:03:18.200
that someone saw you using my name to demand tribute.

726
01:03:18.200 --> 01:03:21.840
They also saw you kill the Siao merchants to silence them.

727
01:03:23.800 --> 01:03:28.760
- Is it true? - Did he tell you... who informed him?

728
01:03:29.800 --> 01:03:32.560
Someone like Mueang Fah would never let it slip.

729
01:03:34.880 --> 01:03:36.520
That damn Mueang Fah.

730
01:03:37.640 --> 01:03:39.440
He keeps finding ways to cause me trouble at every turn.

731
01:03:39.440 --> 01:03:42.800
If you hadn't shown him a weakness to exploit,

732
01:03:42.800 --> 01:03:45.040
you wouldn't have to be angry now.

733
01:03:48.600 --> 01:03:50.240
My apologies, brother.

734
01:03:50.240 --> 01:03:53.560
I'll be more careful from now on.

735
01:03:54.240 --> 01:03:56.440
Make sure no one learns of this.

736
01:03:57.600 --> 01:04:00.680
Or we'll die like those merchants.

737
01:04:02.120 --> 01:04:04.440
If Mueang Fah doesn't speak,

738
01:04:04.440 --> 01:04:06.360
no one will know.

739
01:04:07.320 --> 01:04:09.320
But who knows...

740
01:04:10.360 --> 01:04:12.280
how trustworthy he really is?

741
01:04:14.160 --> 01:04:18.200
Honestly, I can't stand him.

742
01:04:18.200 --> 01:04:20.960
He doesn't seem to be of much help to us.

743
01:04:20.960 --> 01:04:23.480
Now that he knows our secret,

744
01:04:23.480 --> 01:04:24.880
we can trust him even less.

745
01:04:24.880 --> 01:04:27.160
Since we can't fully trust him,

746
01:04:27.160 --> 01:04:29.440
we need to keep him close.

747
01:04:30.440 --> 01:04:33.600
I know Mueang Fah's weakness better than anyone.

748
01:04:36.240 --> 01:04:38.960
He's still useful to us.

749
01:04:39.560 --> 01:04:42.160
Let's not let a trivial matter ruin our big plan.

750
01:04:44.600 --> 01:04:47.120
I assured him it wasn't true.

751
01:04:47.120 --> 01:04:49.560
Stay calm and don't admit a thing.

752
01:04:49.560 --> 01:04:51.320
It will die down soon enough.

753
01:04:52.920 --> 01:04:57.360
Soon, we will both be kings.

754
01:04:58.280 --> 01:05:00.720
Ullavee and Wiang Merng Mang

755
01:05:00.720 --> 01:05:02.920
will rise together.

756
01:05:31.440 --> 01:05:35.360
I've prepared everything needed for the ceremony.

757
01:05:35.360 --> 01:05:37.600
The venue is beautiful.

758
01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:40.640
There's nothing to worry about with the Soul-Blessing Ceremony.

759
01:05:41.440 --> 01:05:44.400
Thank you ever so much, seer.

760
01:05:44.400 --> 01:05:46.320
You're most welcome, Your Highness.

761
01:05:49.320 --> 01:05:50.640
Wait.

762
01:05:59.400 --> 01:06:01.640
I bow before you, Royal Consort Chiang La-or.

763
01:06:03.000 --> 01:06:04.920
I have a question.

764
01:06:04.920 --> 01:06:09.000
Why is Mueang Fah still here? Why hasn't he left for the border?

765
01:06:09.000 --> 01:06:14.840
Won't his staying here bring bad luck to Ullavee?

766
01:06:16.080 --> 01:06:18.480
Don't think about that just yet, Mother.

767
01:06:19.120 --> 01:06:22.120
Let's focus on my bedding ceremony.

768
01:06:22.120 --> 01:06:27.120
I don't want someone else to ruin our ceremony.

769
01:06:29.520 --> 01:06:32.520
But if you have no objection,

770
01:06:32.520 --> 01:06:35.280
I won't press it.

771
01:06:35.280 --> 01:06:40.920
Either way, I truly appreciate you taking care of everything.

772
01:06:42.960 --> 01:06:44.120
Of course.

773
01:07:22.600 --> 01:07:24.640
Look.

774
01:07:29.680 --> 01:07:33.160
Lady Fongnuan, that's impressive.

775
01:07:33.160 --> 01:07:36.600
You use different-colored threads.

776
01:07:36.600 --> 01:07:40.600
You've made these Hawk's Eye Amulets unusually beautiful.

777
01:07:41.280 --> 01:07:42.520
Isn't this chic?

778
01:07:43.240 --> 01:07:44.360
Chic?

779
01:07:45.520 --> 01:07:46.760
Chic?

780
01:07:46.760 --> 01:07:49.800
Do you think you can do the same?

781
01:07:49.800 --> 01:07:51.360
Yes, my lady.

782
01:07:52.200 --> 01:07:57.360
Could you take over from here? I'll hang this in the ceremony pavilion

783
01:07:57.360 --> 01:07:59.280
so we can see how many we'll need.

784
01:07:59.280 --> 01:08:00.440
Of course.

785
01:08:25.720 --> 01:08:27.440
You've been through a lot.

786
01:08:28.640 --> 01:08:30.280
Are you talking to me?

787
01:08:33.400 --> 01:08:35.680
You lost your parents

788
01:08:35.680 --> 01:08:37.680
and the people you loved.

789
01:08:37.680 --> 01:08:39.560
Your boyfriend sucks.

790
01:08:39.560 --> 01:08:41.280
Your friend betrayed you.

791
01:08:52.440 --> 01:08:53.720
Am I right?

792
01:08:54.840 --> 01:08:56.560
Then that's how it is.

793
01:08:57.400 --> 01:08:59.040
You're right.

794
01:08:59.040 --> 01:09:00.840
How did you know?

795
01:09:00.840 --> 01:09:03.040
Are you a fortune teller?

796
01:09:05.400 --> 01:09:08.040
Some things are part of us.

797
01:09:08.600 --> 01:09:12.440
Our lives are more than what we see.

798
01:09:13.880 --> 01:09:16.120
There are also things...

799
01:09:16.920 --> 01:09:18.400
we cannot see.

800
01:09:29.800 --> 01:09:31.640
If you wish for something,

801
01:09:31.640 --> 01:09:36.200
Take this cone inside and make a wish at the ancestral shrine.

802
01:09:51.000 --> 01:09:52.880
That's the fortune-teller uncle.

803
01:10:01.240 --> 01:10:02.800
Fortune teller!

804
01:10:05.880 --> 01:10:07.080
Uncle!

805
01:10:10.240 --> 01:10:11.760
Where did he go?

806
01:10:59.680 --> 01:11:00.480
I'll see you [Next Episode]

807
01:11:00.480 --> 01:11:01.920
at Prince Kong Tai's birthday celebration.

808
01:11:01.920 --> 01:11:03.600
Enjoy yourself.

809
01:11:03.600 --> 01:11:05.320
I've taken care of everything.

810
01:11:05.320 --> 01:11:06.640
Cheers!

811
01:11:06.640 --> 01:11:08.200
Move!

812
01:11:08.200 --> 01:11:09.480
Do you wish to die?

813
01:11:09.480 --> 01:11:12.600
My lady, you look beautiful.

814
01:11:12.600 --> 01:11:13.800
Prince Mueang Fah.

815
01:11:13.800 --> 01:11:17.080
Thanks to you, I no longer wish to die.

816
01:11:17.080 --> 01:11:19.560
May your love grow ever stronger and last forever.

817
01:11:19.560 --> 01:11:22.160
May you be blessed with many children and grandchildren.

818
01:11:22.160 --> 01:11:23.560
Please take care of my sister.

819
01:11:23.560 --> 01:11:24.880
Please get out of my life.

820
01:11:24.880 --> 01:11:26.040
We shouldn't see each other again.

821
01:11:26.040 --> 01:11:27.640
Do you not love me anymore?

822
01:11:27.640 --> 01:11:29.240
What a modest celebration.

823
01:11:29.240 --> 01:11:32.680
Quite fitting for a consort from a little place like Wang Nam Lin.

824
01:11:32.680 --> 01:11:36.080
Once I'm king, I can give anyone whatever they want.

825
01:11:36.080 --> 01:11:37.760
Or do you disagree?

826
01:11:39.480 --> 01:11:41.280
Bew!

827
01:11:41.280 --> 01:11:42.760
Do you know him?
